{
  "commands": {
    "api-keys create": "Mint an API Key (raw secret surfaced once only).

Usage:
  splitch api-keys create [flags]

Flags:
  --app <app>              [type: string; default: SPLITCH_APP or config] App ID or slug.
  --env <environment>      [type: string; default: SPLITCH_ENV or config] Environment ID or key.
  --by <mode>              [type: string; default: automatic] Allowed: id. Resolve a canonical-looking selector explicitly.
  --body-json <json>       [type: JSON object; default: none] Request body fields; see Request body below.
  --idempotency-key <key>  [type: string; default: generated] Stable retry key for this mutation.
  --output-file <path>     [type: string; default: none] Write the once-only secret to a new 0600 file instead of stdout; the payload reports valueWrittenTo.
  --json                   [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help               [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Request body (--body-json):
  scopes           required  string ("data-plane:evaluate" | "data-plane:write")[]
  idempotency_key  optional  string
  Example:
    {"scopes":[]}

Credential semantics:
  API Key is secret and server-side only; a newly created value is shown once and cannot be read back.

Example:
  splitch api-keys create --body-json '{"scopes":[]}' --json",
    "api-keys list": "List API Key metadata (no secrets; bounded; reports its own truncation).

Usage:
