    "flags get": "Get a Flag definition by canonical ID or key. Returns complete per-Environment Flag Configurations and running Experiment references by default; omit envs for every Environment in the App.

Usage:
  splitch flags get <flag-id-or-key> [flags]

Flags:
  --app <app>          [type: string; default: SPLITCH_APP or config] App ID or slug.
  --env <environment>  [type: string; default: none] Limit hydrated Configurations to one Environment; flags list --summary selects its compact Configuration.
  --by <mode>          [type: string; default: automatic] Allowed: id or key. Resolve a canonical-looking selector explicitly.
  --summary            [type: boolean; default: false] Print compact human columns instead of complete per-Environment Configurations; cannot be combined with --json.
  --json               [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help           [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch flags get <flag-id-or-key> --json",
    "flags list": "List Flag definitions in an App (bounded; reports its own truncation). Returns complete per-Environment Flag Configurations and running Experiment references by default; omit envs for every Environment in the App.

Usage:
  splitch flags list [flags]

Flags:
  --app <app>          [type: string; default: SPLITCH_APP or config] App ID or slug.
  --env <environment>  [type: string; default: none] Limit hydrated Configurations to one Environment; flags list --summary selects its compact Configuration.
  --summary            [type: boolean; default: false] Print compact human columns instead of complete per-Environment Configurations; cannot be combined with --json.
  --json               [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help           [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch flags list --json",
    "flags promote": "Promote selected Flag Configuration field-groups between Environments.

Usage:
  splitch flags promote <flag-id-or-key> [flags]

Flags:
  --app <app>                 [type: string; default: SPLITCH_APP or config] App ID or slug.
  --env <environment>         [type: string; default: SPLITCH_ENV or config] Environment ID or key.
  --by <mode>                 [type: string; default: automatic] Allowed: id. Resolve a canonical-looking selector explicitly.
  --from-environment-id <id>  [type: string; default: none] Source Environment ID.
  --body-json <json>          [type: JSON object; default: none] Request body fields; see Request body below.
  --idempotency-key <key>     [type: string; default: generated] Stable retry key for this mutation.
  --confirm                   [type: boolean; default: false] Approve and apply a Policy-gated change.
  --json                      [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help                  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Request body (--body-json):
  fromEnvironmentId  required  string
  select             required  { availability?: string[]; targeting?: true; rollout?: true; enabled?: true }
  review             optional  { action: "approve_and_apply" }
  idempotency_key    required  string
  Example:
    {"fromEnvironmentId":"fromEnvironment_1","select":{"availability":[],"targeting":true,"rollout":true,"enabled":true},"idempotency_key":"idem-1"}

Example:
  splitch flags promote <flag-id-or-key> --body-json '{"fromEnvironmentId":"fromEnvironment_1","select":{"availability":[],"targeting":true,"rollout":true,"enabled":true},"idempotency_key":"idem-1"}' --json",
