  "meta": {
    "context": "Show the logged-in principal and the resolved App and Environment.

Usage:
  splitch context [flags]

Flags:
  --app <app>          [type: string; default: SPLITCH_APP or config] App ID or slug.
  --env <environment>  [type: string; default: SPLITCH_ENV or config] Environment ID or key.
  --json               [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help           [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch context --json",
    "health": "Check the Control Plane API health endpoint.

Usage:
  splitch health [flags]

Flags:
  --endpoint <url>  [type: URL; default: resolved platform target origin] Control Plane API base URL.
  --json            [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help        [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch health --json",
    "login": "Authenticate the control-plane session with the browser device flow.

Usage:
  splitch login [--app <app>] [flags]

Flags:
  --app <app>  [type: string; default: SPLITCH_APP or config] App ID or slug.
  --json       [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help   [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch login",
    "logout": "Revoke and remove the stored control-plane session.

Usage:
  splitch logout [flags]

Flags:
  --json      [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch logout --json",
    "use": "Select the default App and Environment for the current directory.

Usage:
  splitch use [--app <app>] [--env <environment>] [flags]

Flags:
  --app <app>          [type: string; default: unchanged] App ID or slug.
  --env <environment>  [type: string; default: unchanged] Environment ID or key.
  --json               [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help           [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch use --app checkout --env dev --json",
  },
  "root": "splitch - feature flags and A/B experimentation from your terminal

Usage:
  splitch <command> [flags]
  splitch <resource> <action> [arguments] [flags]

Commands:
  login           Authenticate the control-plane session with the browser device flow.
  logout          Revoke and remove the stored control-plane session.
  use             Select the default App and Environment for the current directory.
  context         Show the logged-in principal and the resolved App and Environment.
  health          Check the Control Plane API health endpoint.

Resource groups:
  api-keys
  app-attention-rollup
  app-members
  approval-request-reviews
  approval-requests
  apps
  client-key
  cloudflare
  cloudflare-installations
  convex-installations
  env-policy
  environment-exposure-status
  envs
  event-definition-versions
  event-definitions
  experiment-results
  experiments
  flag-config
  flag-targeting-rules
  flag-variants
  flags
  metrics
  organization-members
  organization-usage
  orgs
  runs
  segments
  sentry-installations
  sentry-secret-rotations

Flags:
  -v, --version  [type: boolean; default: false] Show the installed CLI version and exit.
  -h, --help     [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Credential semantics:
  Client Key  Public data-plane key for browsers, mobile apps, and other untrusted clients.
  API Key     Secret data-plane key for trusted servers; a newly created value is shown once.

Start here:
  splitch login

Run \`splitch <command> --help\` or \`splitch <resource> <action> --help\` for details.",
}
`;
